  "notes": "Northern Ndebele (isiNdebele, Zimbabwe) — Nguni Bantu language, Guthrie S.44, close relative of Zulu. Shares Zulu's three click series — dental (c/ǀ), alveolar (q/ǃ), lateral (x/ǁ) — each with plain, aspirated, and voiced (prenasalized/depressor) variants, plus ejective affricates (tj, ts, kl) not present in standard Zulu. Prenasalized consonants (mb, nd, ng, nj, nz…) are single phonemes. Five-vowel system a/e/i/o/u. Tone is phonemically high/low but unmarked in the standard orthography.",
